    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.degree_mixing_dict - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.degree_mixing_dict.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.degree_mixing_dict()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Count edges by the degrees of their two endpoints.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.degree_mixing_dict()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Count edges by the degrees of their two endpoints.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.degree_mixing_dict()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Count edges by the degrees of their two endpoints.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCount edges by the degrees of their two endpoints.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L37111-L37204){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.degree_mixing_dict(\n    source_mode=\"out\",\n    target_mode=\"in\",\n    weighted=None,\n    normalized=False,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Degree mixing dict](../assets/graphs/degree-mixing-dict.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"The hub-and-leaf graph with each degree in a badge. The four accent edges join degree 1 to degree 3, and the hub edge C–D joins 3 to 3. Counting every edge from both ends gives {1: {3: 4}, 3: {1: 4, 3: 2}}.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nFor every pair of degrees `(j, k)`, how many edges run from a node of degree `j` to a\nnode of degree `k`. This joint degree distribution is the raw material of degree\nassortativity: if edges concentrate along `j = k`, similar nodes link to each other.\nUndirected edges are counted from both ends, so the table is symmetric; on a directed\ngraph each edge is counted once, from its source's `source_mode` degree to its target's\n`target_mode` degree. See `degree_mixing_matrix()` for the same counts as a matrix.\nMatches NetworkX's `degree_mixing_dict()`.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[source_mode]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[&quot;out&quot;]{.st}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   On directed graphs, the degree of each edge's source: `\"out\"` (default) or `\"in\"`.\n\n<code>[target_mode]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[&quot;in&quot;]{.st}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   On directed graphs, the degree of each edge's target: `\"in\"` (default) or `\"out\"`.\n\n<code>[weighted]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Whether degrees are weighted (sums of edge weights). If `None` (default), follows the\n    graph.\n\n<code>[normalized]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, return fractions of all counted edge ends instead of counts. Default is\n    `False`.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [dict]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   A nested dictionary `{j: {k: count}}`, both levels sorted. Every degree that appears\n    is a key.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~degree_mixing_matrix`) \n\n:   The same counts as a matrix.\n\n[](`~attribute_mixing_dict`) \n\n:   Count links by an attribute instead of degree.\n\n[](`~assortativity_degree`) \n\n:   The correlation of these counts.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nEach link counts once from each end. `C` has three neighbors and links to `A` and `B`,\nwith two each, and to `D`, with one:\n\n::: {#ccd4df8a .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"A\", \"C\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\")]\n)\n\ngraph.degree_mixing_dict()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n{1: {3: 1}, 2: {2: 2, 3: 2}, 3: {1: 1, 2: 2}}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### The popular five\n\n`friends()` links 24 members of two clubs in a made-up town, a chess club and a climbing\nclub, who are friends. Five of them have five friends each, the most anyone has: Ben,\nHugo, Jules, Oona and Tara. Counting each friendship from both ends, 14 of their 25 end\nat another of the five:\n\n::: {#83d97c89 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfriends = ec.friends()\n\nfriends.degree_mixing_dict()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n{2: {4: 2},\n 3: {3: 22, 4: 10, 5: 7},\n 4: {2: 2, 3: 10, 4: 4, 5: 4},\n 5: {3: 7, 4: 4, 5: 14}}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThey make 7 of the 10 possible friendships among themselves:\n\n::: {#14bbb246 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfive = [\"Ben\", \"Hugo\", \"Jules\", \"Oona\", \"Tara\"]\namong = [\n    (u, v) for i, u in enumerate(five) for v in five[i + 1 :]\n    if friends.has_edge(u, v)\n]\n\nfriends.plot(\n    highlight=among, size_by=\"degree\", color_by=\"club\",\n    label_by=\"label\", seed=8,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }